---
title = "Documentation"
summary = "Learn how to use Caffeine to define service expectations and generate reliability artifacts."
---

There exist three levels of configurations, each distinct and isolated, referenced by lower levels via unique naming scheme and typically owned by different _roles_ within an organization:

(1) *Artifacts*: defined by standard library or plugin developers per distinct reliability artifact.

(2) *Blueprints*: defined by observability experts per artifact abstraction referencing artifacts.

(3) *Expectations*: defined by the operating team per service referencing blueprints.

{.figure}
![stardust](/images/documentation_structure_of_configs.png)

An example of how the file types interact across a typical engineering organization

Thus, for the *SLO* artifact, we might see something like this:

{.figure}
![stardust](/images/documentation_structure_of_configs_filled_in.png)

The same diagram from above with made of examples for the SLO reliability artifact

The documentation is split by _persona_ with sufficient details for each to operate within their domain.

