## Service Owners

### Service Expectation Explained

*Definition:* a service expectation is single blueprint invocation for a single service within the domain of an owning team. 

The organization name, team name, and service name are baked in to the filepath path: 

`ORGANIZATION_NAME/TEAM_NAME/SERIVE_NAME.yaml`

As all other configurations, an expectation is a `.yaml` file with the following required fields.

``` =html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Attribute</th>
      <th>Expected Type</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>name</td>
      <td>String</td>
      <td>Unique within a single <code>artifacts.yaml</code> file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>blueprint</td>
      <td>String</td>
      <td>An identifier referencing a blueprint.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>inputs</td>
      <td>Dict(String, Any)</td>
      <td>Collection of input names mapped to input values.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```

So, an example would look like:

```
expectations:
  - name: "Admin Portal Home Page LCP Latency"
    blueprint: LCP_Latency
    inputs:
      - view: /admin/home
        p95_latency_in_seconds: 5
        threshold: 99.5%
```

### Documentation and Distribution

Caffeine has no opinion on where these files live, just the file path as mentioned above. Documentation might be generated as part of compilation depending on the artifact.

